# Bacillus anthracis MLVA-25 of Lista et al. 2006 (BMC Microbiol 6:33). The panel is the eight
# MLVA-8 loci of Keim et al. 2000 and seventeen bams loci; the publication reports it as 21 loci
# from earlier work plus four new ones (bams34, bams44, bams51 and bams53), and drops bams7 of
# the MLVA-20 set because its alleles are too long for capillary sizing.
#
# The paper gives no primer sequences: it cites Le Fleche et al. and Keim et al. for the 21 older
# loci and the GPMS database for the four new ones. The primers here are therefore the MLVAbank
# ones already bundled as bacillus_mlva31_mlvabank, of which this panel is the first 25 loci, with
# the same search windows. Those windows are wide on purpose; the sizes Lista et al. observed are
# narrower and are recorded in markers.tsv.
#
# The order is the one the Methods uses for the MLVA-8 code, vrrA first and the two plasmid loci
# last, followed by the bams loci in numerical order, so the first eight digits of a profile line
# up with bacillus_mlva8_keim_2000.

vrrA	CACAACTACCACCGATGGCACA	GCGCGTTTCGTTTGATTCATAC	64-764
vrrB1	ATAGGTGGTTTTCCGCAAGTTATTC	GATGAGTTTGATAAAGAATAGCCTGTG	60-679
vrrB2	CACAGGCTATTCTTTATCAAACTCATC	CCCAAGGTGAAGATTGTTGTTGA	60-603
vrrC1	GAAGCAAGAAAGTGATGTAGTGGAC	CATTTCCTCAAGTGCTACAGGTTC	330-1030
vrrC2	CCAGAAGAAGTGGAACCTGTAGCAC	GTCTTTCCATTAATCGCGCTCTATC	282-982
CG3	TGTCGTTTTACTTCTCTCTCCAATAC	AGTCATTGTTCTGTATAAAGGGCAT	60-608
pXO1-aat	CAATTTATTAACGATCAGATTAAGTTCA	TCTAGAATTAGTTGCTTCATAATGGC	60-576
pXO2-at	TCATCCTCTTTTAAGTCTTGGGT	GTGTGATGAACTCCGACGACA	60-591
bams01	GTTGAGCATGAGAGGTACCTTGTCCTTTTT	AGTTCAAGCGCCAGAAGGTTATGAGTTATC	235-935
bams03	GCAGCAACAGAAAACTTCTCTCCAATAACA	TCCTCCCTGAGAACTGCTATCACCTTTAAC	299-999
bams05	GCAGGAAGAACAAAAGAAACTAGAAGAGCA	ATTATTAGCAGGGGCCTCTCCTGCATTACC	60-757
bams13	AATTGAGAAATTGCTGTACCAAACT	CTAGTGCATTTGACCCTAATCTTGT	564-1264
bams15	GTATTTCCCCCAGATACAGTAATCC	GTGTACATGTTGATTCATGCTGTTT	168-868
bams21	TGTAGTGCCAGATTTGTCTTCTGTA	CAAATTTTGAGATGGGAGTTTTACT	426-1126
